# ============================================================================
#  Line endings, declared rather than left to whoever cloned it.
#
#  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `install.bat` is stored in this repository with
#  LF-only line endings, and on disk it has CRLF. That difference is not
#  cosmetic: cmd.exe reads a batch file by BYTE OFFSET, and with LF endings
#  a `goto` past a label can land mid-line and run something else. ATK hit
#  exactly this on 2026-08-07, when every .bat in that project was rewritten
#  with LF and install.bat failed halfway through a wipe. ATK's own
#  .gitattributes has said `*.bat text eol=crlf` ever since; this repo has
#  never had one, so what a fresh clone gets has depended on the cloner's
#  `core.autocrlf` — which is to say, on luck.
#
#  Renormalise the working tree after adding this file:
#      git add --renormalize .
# ============================================================================

*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

*.py    text eol=lf
*.pyi   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.cfg   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# Word documents are a zip. Never touch them.
*.docx  binary
*.doc   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
